{"id": "EUVD-2026-105082", "enisaUuid": "06c10c91-5964-3e6a-a482-776410eb852f", "description": "Ghidra 10.2 through 12.1.4 contains a denial of service vulnerability in the ELF loader's ElfHeader class that allocates arrays sized by unvalidated extended section and program header counts. Attackers can supply a crafted 128-byte ELF file that triggers an OutOfMemoryError during load-spec discovery at import or in headless analysis pipelines.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:19:49", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/commit/6c50a66e8a939e2bcbaf0a6432ec5d53a41ceeb3", "https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/Ghidra_12.1.4_build/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/ElfHeader.java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ghidra-10.2-through-12.1.4-denial-of-service-via-elf-loader-extended-header-counts"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j4jr-xgjh-hpvc", "CVE-2026-113604"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5108206c-5aca-325c-9340-3d9f7555aba7", "product": {"name": "Ghidra", "vendor": {"name": "NSA"}}, "product_version": "10.2 \u226412.1.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "291d1a9f-9b91-3468-947d-f804bc5382e1", "vendor": {"name": "NationalSecurityAgency"}}], "isExploited": false}